                                "sense_id": "3d8fe8ee-d8d5-3b7c-8aec-c77d7f019f48",
                                "text": "The signalese for 'S/L' I could decipher, but the NMI defeated me, until I learned that it referred to the fact, an oddity to Americans, that I had 'No Middle Initial'."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb2b16cd-ee57-49fd-b28c-9bef3e25283c",
                                "sense_id": "3d8fe8ee-d8d5-3b7c-8aec-c77d7f019f48",
                                "text": "The signal \"dit-dah-dit- dit-dit\" which, in signalese meant \"wait\", was heard a lot while we attempted to decipher what it was the operator on the other end"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e7066c6b-3ce5-439b-853e-d4da1f19dd5c",
                                "sense_id": "3d8fe8ee-d8d5-3b7c-8aec-c77d7f019f48",
                                "text": "The commodore's staff prepares the necessary message using a standardised jargon used by the Navy, sometimes referred to as 'signalese'."
                            }
                        ]
